    "body": "claimed: bherbruck (Claude Code session) · 2026-11-08T01:54:10Z · branch issue/230-snug-cylinder (fork bherbruck/Camcraft) · plan: Fit to Models' cylinder takes its radius from the models' largest horizontal distance from the fit's XY centre (the revolved max radius for a turned part) plus the margin, instead of the footprint's diagonal - still containing every vertex, never larger than before; pin: a round part's fitted bar is R + allowance. Applies to any cylinder fit (a snugger cylinder that still contains the part is right for a mill too). Outside contributor without label rights - please add `claimed`.",
