    "body": "progress: bherbruck · 2026-11-08T01:58:01Z · fix committed on issue/230-snug-cylinder (fork): Fit to Models' cylinder radius = the models' largest horizontal distance from the fit's axis (`model::solid_world_radius_about`) + the margin (`stock::fit_cylinder_about`) - a round R part gets R + allowance; still contains every vertex, never larger than the old diagonal. Pinned by `stock::tests::a_snug_cylinder_is_the_revolved_radius_plus_the_allowance` and `shell::a_cylinder_fit_round_a_turned_part_is_snug` (r10 bar + 2 mm → 24 mm); `shell::cylinder_fit_keeps_the_cylinder_choice` updated (a cube's half-diagonal + margin). Existing documents keep their stock numbers; only a new Fit is snugger. Gate running; PR follows. (PR #238 refactors the same StockFit handler a few lines away - a trivial merge either way.)",
